.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]mode\f[R] string is heap\-allocated via \f[CR]strdup()\f[R].
Always call \f[CR]bc_debug_status_free()\f[R] to avoid memory leaks.
.IP \(bu 2
When the debugger is not active, \f[CR]mode\f[R] is set to
\f[CR]\(dqrun\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]breakpoints\f[R] is 0, and
\f[CR]depth\f[R] is 0.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]depth\f[R] field reflects the nesting level at the point the
status was queried.
If execution is stopped at a breakpoint, this is the depth of the
stopped command.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: the client library is not thread\-safe.
